#' Select variants
#'
#' Selects variants on the map: by a query (such as "missense at 40-80 with se < 0.2", "lower
#' and not robust", "from C in feature disulfide", "in Core and not in Surface"), by name or by
#' position; replaces the selection or adds to, intersects or subtracts from it; optionally
#' saves it by name (with its query). A query that needs the run's robustness checks it first.
#' Shows the Map view with the selection.
#'
#' @param condition A condition by name or number (from 1), when the design has more than one;
#' the first if not given. Optional; a string.
#' @param contrast A contrast between conditions (its name, or its number from 1): select on
#' its differential map. Optional; a string.
#' @param filter Only these of them: scored, low (low confidence), filtered or missing.
#' Optional; a string.
#' @param operation What to do with the selection there is: replace (the default), add,
#' intersect or subtract. Optional; a string.
#' @param positions Positions on the target (numbered from 1): every substitution there.
#' Optional; a vector of whole numbers (Python: a list).
#' @param query A query of MaveScape's selection language: kinds (missense, nonsense,
#' synonymous), states (scored, low, filtered, missing), at/pos/refpos with positions, from/to
#' with residues or groups, score/se/q/replicates/input compared with a number,
#' lower/higher/neutral, robustness verdicts (robust, fragile, uncertain, borderline,
#' size-dependent, sometimes-scored, "class depends on the pseudocount"), feature with a name,
#' in with a saved selection's name, selected, and, or, not, parentheses. Optional; a string.
#' @param run A score run by name ("Run 2") or id; the latest run of the current design if not
#' given. Optional; a string.
#' @param save_as Save the selection under this name. Optional; a string.
#' @param variants MAVE-HGVS names, such as p.Trp36Ala. Optional; a vector of strings (Python:
#' a list).
#' @param ms A connection from ms_connect() (default: the last one made).
#' @return A mavescape_result: the message and the data MaveScape answered with.
#' @export
ms_select_variants <- function(condition = NULL, contrast = NULL, filter = NULL, operation = NULL, positions = NULL, query = NULL, run = NULL, save_as = NULL, variants = NULL, ms = ms_default()) {
  ms_call("select_variants", condition = condition, contrast = contrast, filter = filter, operation = operation, positions = .ms_array(positions), query = query, run = run, save_as = save_as, variants = .ms_array(variants), ms = ms)
}

